{`id`: "axhard-a-20261015/ProcessingRecord/H21", `type`: "ProcessingRecord", `properties`: {`id`: "axhard-a-20261015/ProcessingRecord/H21", `fixture_id`: "axhard-a-20261015", `data_status`: "FICTIONAL", `report_id`: "H21", `name`: "H21 processing", `processing_status`: "COMPLETE", `cap_omitted`: false, `output_file`: "evidence/combined_output_A.json", `output_path`: "$.reports[20]", `retained_idea_count`: 1}},
{`id`: "axhard-a-20261015/Paragraph/H21.p1", `type`: "Paragraph", `properties`: {`id`: "axhard-a-20261015/Paragraph/H21.p1", `fixture_id`: "axhard-a-20261015", `data_status`: "FICTIONAL", `paragraph_id`: "H21.p1", `name`: "H21.p1", `position`: 1, `text`: "For the two AI-chip businesses, I expect NOVA to outperform DRAG from 1 November to 1 December 2026. NovaChips has a more balanced customer list, while DragonLogic relies heavily on one delayed project. That makes the relative position attractive to me, but the whole sector could lose value if customers tighten their capital budgets. I would keep the trade small because a broad rally or selloff could dominate both companies' operating news.", `text_sha256`: "bf27a656864045d6e62c79683162c650db623f8082555ac22d0f957123cd2516", `input_path`: "$.reports[20].paragraphs[0]"}},
